=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play users/sudo-password -------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the User Management screen proposed for$
# slice 5, drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (users.Admin.Check, users.ReadElevation, sudoers.Read,$
# PolicyOf, Invoker, ssh.ReadPAM), each grant the real$
# sudoers.PlanFor on the real plan/apply engine. Creating a user$
# and the keys are the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build.$
# Nothing on this machine changes: every command and file is the$
# fake's.$
$
# Info: users/sudo-password$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. george has a password and$
# sudo by hardn-grant-george asking for it.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take them away$
   2) Don't ask password   For admin rights$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 2$
$
# Don't ask password ###########################################$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
$
   -  Stop asking george's password$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-grant-george$
      @@ -1,2 +1,2 @@$
       # Managed by hardn$
      -george ALL=(ALL) ALL$
      +george ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL$
$
  Stop asking george's password for admin rights? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Stop asking george's password  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-grant-george kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take them away$
   2) Ask for password     For admin rights$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: users/sudo-password$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Stop asking george's password$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-grant-george$
$

